        "body": "## Summary  - Stack on #99700 to add the next policy doctor repair slice. - Wire automatic repairs for channel ingress narrowing findings:   - `policy/ingress-open-groups-denied` sets reported `groupPolicy` paths to `allowlist`.   - `policy/ingress-group-mention-required` sets reported `requireMention` paths to `true`. - Keep the existing `workspaceRepairs=true` opt-in and finding fix-class gate, and only patch the exact `oc://openclaw.config/...` path emitted by policy detection.  ## Validation  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.test.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/metadata.test.ts --reporter=dot` (292 tests) - `pnpm exec oxfmt --check extensions/policy/src/doctor/automatic-repairs.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/scopes/channels.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.test.ts` - `pnpm exec oxlint extensions/policy/src/doctor/automatic-repairs.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/scopes/channels.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.test.ts` - `pnpm tsgo:extensions` - `git diff --check` - `codex review --base origin/policy-doctor-required-deny-repairs` (clean; first shorter run timed out before result)  ## Stack  - Stacked on #99700 / #99690 / #99686 / #99121. - Review after #99700, then rebase onto `main` as the lower stack lands.  ## Not Run  - `pnpm tsgo:core` remains locally blocked by unrelated untracked `src/oc-path/` unused-symbol errors in this worktree.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior or issue addressed:\n`doctor --fix` repairs channel ingress narrowing findings by setting reported `groupPolicy` paths to `allowlist` and reported `requireMention` paths to `true`, gated by `workspaceRepairs=true`.\n\nReal environment tested:\nWindows PowerShell in `C:\\src\\openclaw-fork` on the restacked policy series, top head `283c1bb4ca` and this PR head `5d39a7e932`. This is a source-harness proof; it does not start a packaged OpenClaw binary or make live LLM calls.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n1. `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/policy/src/doctor/metadata.test.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.test.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/strictness.test.ts src/flows/doctor-repair-flow.test.ts --reporter=dot`\n2. `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs test/scripts/plugin-sdk-surface-report.test.ts --reporter=dot`\n3. `pnpm tsgo:extensions`\n4. `pnpm lint:extensions`\n5. `git diff --check`\n\nEvidence after fix:\nThe focused policy/core Vitest run passed 10 core repair-flow tests and 297 policy doctor tests, including `repairs automatic channel ingress narrowing findings` and `does not repair channel ingress config without workspace repair opt-in`. The SDK surface tooling test passed 7 tests. `tsgo:extensions`, `lint:extensions`, and `git diff --check` all exited 0.\n\nObserved result after fix:\nChannel ingress repairs apply only to the exact `oc://openclaw.config/...` paths emitted by policy detection and do not run without workspace repair opt-in.\n\nWhat was not tested:\nNo packaged CLI smoke, live provider run, or live LLM call was run for this source-harness proof.\n",
